-- title:
--   F-vector dévissage of the generic fibre after faithfully flat base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring that is a domain, let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and assume $p$ is irreducible in $R$ (a uniformiser). Let $H$ be a commutative Hopf algebra over $R$ which is finite and flat as an $R$-module and whose comultiplication is cocommutative, and let $n$ be a natural number such that for every commutative $R$-algebra $T$ every element $f$ of the convolution group `WithConv (H →ₐ[R] T)` of $R$-algebra maps $H \to T$ satisfies $f^{p^n} = 1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a discrete valuation domain $R_2$, together with an $R$-algebra structure making $R_2$ faithfully flat over $R$, and a field $K_2$ that is a fraction field of $R_2$, such that $p$ is irreducible in $R_2$ and the $K_2$-Hopf algebra $K_2 \otimes_{R_2} (R_2 \otimes_R H)$ satisfies [`HopfAlgebra.HasFVectDevissage R₂ K₂ p`](def/HopfAlgebra_HasFVectDevissage.html#L10). The latter is the inductively defined predicate generated by: (nil) any $A$ with $\dim_{K_2} A = 1$; and (step) any finite cocommutative $K_2$-Hopf algebra $A$ admitting a surjective bialgebra map $\pi : A \to \bar A$ onto a finite cocommutative $K_2$-Hopf algebra $\bar A$ already satisfying the predicate, for which there are $r \geq 1$, a finite field $F$ with $|F| = p^r$ such that $p^r - 1$ is a unit in $R_2$, a group homomorphism $\chi : F^\times \to R_2^\times$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota : F \to R_2/\mathfrak m$ with $\chi(l)$ reducing to $\iota(l)$ for all $l$, such that the Hopf kernel $\mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi$ — the equalizer of the coaction of $\pi$ and $a \mapsto a \otimes 1$ into $A \otimes_{K_2} \bar A$ — has $K_2$-dimension $p^r$ and carries an `FVectStructure F K₂`, i.e. a map $F \to$ bialgebra endomorphisms sending $1$ to the identity, multiplication to composition, $0$ to the convolution unit and addition to convolution multiplication.
--
--   This is the form in which Raynaud's result on finite flat group schemes killed by $p^n$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$ is used: after a faithfully flat extension of the base, the generic fibre becomes a successive extension of one-dimensional $F$-vector space schemes, with the requisite fundamental characters available in the new base. It feeds the surjectivity statement [`HopfAlgebra.surjective_of_injective_of_surjective_baseChange_of_pow_eq_one_of_simple`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.surjective_of_injective_of_surjective_baseChange_of_pow_eq_one_of_simple).
